          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "സംരംഭം — saṁrambhaṁ — \"a venture; an enterprise\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "അവൾ ഒരു ചെറിയ ബേക്കറി സംരംഭം തുടങ്ങി. avaḷ oru ceṟiya bēkkaṟi saṁrambhaṁ tuṭaṅṅi. She started a small bakery venture."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A word of business news; സംരംഭം (saṁrambhaṁ) തുടങ്ങുക, to start a venture."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "സംരംഭം (saṁrambhaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit saṁrambha, which CDIAL glosses as vehemence (CDIAL 12993); Malayalam uses it for an undertaking pursued with zeal."
            }
          ]
        },
